# ============================================================
# CELL 05 — AE3 CONSOLIDATION, POOLED RUV, FINAL PERSISTENCE,
#           PARAMETER ROBUSTNESS, AND ACTION DIAGNOSTICS
#
# Purpose
# -------
# Consolidate the outputs from Cells 02–04 before tables and figures.
#
# This cell performs four tasks:
#
# 1. Pooled Relative Utility Value
#    --------------------------------
#    RUV_scenario_pooled =
#        sum(scenario-conditioning value)
#        /
#        sum(Base-policy regret)
#
#    RUV_policy_pooled =
#        sum(policy value versus no action)
#        /
#        sum(no-action regret)
#
#    Ratios of sums are used instead of means of monthly ratios.
#
# 2. Final AE1–AE2–AE3 persistence
#    --------------------------------
#    Reconstruct raw monthly intersections between:
#      - AE2 statistical + magnitude candidates;
#      - AE3 exploratory or confirmatory gates.
#
#    Persistence is then evaluated on the final intersection for:
#      r = 1, 3, and 6 consecutive months.
#
# 3. AE3 parameter robustness
#    --------------------------------
#    Summarise sign and magnitude stability across the nine
#    combinations of:
#      pi    in {0.60, 0.70, 0.80}
#      gamma in {0.50, 1.00, 2.00}
#
#    This is structural sensitivity, not inferential significance
#    for each parameter combination.
#
# 4. Action diagnostics
#    --------------------------------
#    Quantify:
#      - Base-policy -> scenario-policy transitions;
#      - action increases, decreases, and unchanged actions;
#      - value contributed by each transition;
#      - months with negative scenario-conditioning value.
#
# Scientific scope
# ----------------
# - No forecasts are regenerated.
# - No AE2 or AE3 bootstrap is rerun.
# - The default decision model remains unchanged.
# - The previous Cell 04 summary is retained for provenance.
# - This cell supersedes only its simple final-persistence summary.
# ============================================================

