# ============================================================
# CELL 06 — AE3 BOOTSTRAP WITH POLICY RESELECTION
#
# Purpose
# -------
# Audit AE3 inference by reselecting the Base-conditioned and
# scenario-conditioned actions inside every bootstrap replicate.
#
# Why this is needed
# ------------------
# Cell 04 bootstrapped fixed leave-one-point-out contributions.
# That approach preserved the evaluated contributions but did not
# propagate uncertainty from discrete policy reselection.
#
# This cell implements a weighted cluster bootstrap:
#
# 1. Draw multinomial weights over complete control-point
#    trajectories.
# 2. Use the same weights for:
#       - all forecast months;
#       - Favorable and Unfavorable.
# 3. For each held-out point:
#       - remove all bootstrap copies of that point from training;
#       - reselect the Base-conditioned action;
#       - reselect the scenario-conditioned action;
#       - evaluate both actions on the held-out scenario point.
# 4. Weight the held-out contribution by its bootstrap multiplicity.
#
# Primary estimand
# ----------------
# Scenario-conditioning value:
#
#   SCV = loss(Base-conditioned policy under scenario)
#         - loss(scenario-conditioned policy under scenario)
#
# Positive SCV indicates that scenario conditioning improves
# held-out decision performance.
#
# Inferential outputs
# -------------------
# - Pointwise percentile bootstrap intervals.
# - Scenario-wise centered max-t simultaneous bands.
# - Joint centered max-t simultaneous bands across:
#       * all months within AE1;
#       * Favorable and Unfavorable.
# - Fixed-contribution versus policy-reselection comparison.
# - Final AE1–AE2–AE3 persistence after reselection.
# - Policy-selection instability diagnostics.
# - Favorable versus Unfavorable action agreement.
#
# Scientific interpretation
# -------------------------
# The bootstrap represents spatial resampling uncertainty across
# the available control-point trajectories.
#
# It still does not represent:
# - predictive model uncertainty;
# - observation error;
# - temporal sampling uncertainty;
# - spatial dependence between nearby points;
# - uncertainty in the decision-loss specification.
# ============================================================

from __future__ import annotations

